data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":433,"item_id":"fc_0abf11bc62d09e58016adb5a18d8b88191be44fa2cd71b814e","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"base_input\":\"prior-candidate.json\",\"patches\":[{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/applications/3/bindings\",\"value\":\"Let X be the complete ambient Euclidean product ℝⁿ×ℝ, let Y=ℝ, and define f:X→Y on every pair (x,t) by f(x,t)=t. Instantiate A with the actual subset F=E×[0,1] of X. The ambient projection is defined on all of X, and its image f '' F is exactly [0,1] because E is nonempty.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/applications/3/hypothesis_checks/1\",\"value\":\"The projection f is defined on all of X=ℝⁿ×ℝ (not merely on the subtype/set F). For every ambient pair (x,t),(y,u), |t−u|≤sqrt(|x−y|²+|t−u|²), so it is 1-Lipschitz. Since E is nonempty, f '' (E×[0,1])=[0,1]; this identifies the image in the source theorem with the interval.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/13/kind\",\"value\":\"witness\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/13/declaration\",\"value\":\"After proving in S002 that B_i is bounded and constructing an open interval containing it of length at most ρ_i+η_i, choose that interval as J_i.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/13/from_inputs\",\"value\":[\"M008\"]},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/13/from_local\",\"value\":[]},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/9/declaration\",\"value\":\"Define ν to be the restriction volume.restrict([0,1]) on ambient Borel ℝ. No mass value is part of this definition.\"}]}}"}

